<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republic of Turkey</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Turkish Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> is the modern state founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> after the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Established under the leadership of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</a>, it replaced the sultanate and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> with a secular, nationalist republic centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a>. It marks the end point of the Ottoman Empire's decline and the successor state of its Anatolian core.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey.jpg" alt="Republic of Turkey" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Benbennick (original author) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Turkey.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Grand National Assembly abolished the Sultanate on 1 November 1922, proclaimed the <b>Republic of Turkey</b> on 29 October 1923 and abolished the caliphate in March 1924.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1924 the <b>Republic of Turkey</b> abolished the caliphate.</blockquote><a href="/religion/islam">Islam · Spread</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1928, after the fall of the Ottoman Empire following World War I and the founding of the <b>Republic of Turkey</b>, widespread language reforms instituted by Mustafa Kemal Atatürk, part of the larger framework of Atatürk’s reforms, replaced many Persian and Arabic loanwords with Turkish equivalents and the…</blockquote><a href="/language/ottoman-turkish">Ottoman Turkish · Change &amp; Descendants</a></li><li><blockquote>Kemalism remains the founding ideology of the <b>Republic of Turkey</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/kemalism">Kemalism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1935 the <b>Republic of Turkey</b> under Mustafa Kemal Atatürk made it a museum.</blockquote><a href="/work/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia · Reception</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;İstiklal Marşı&quot; (&quot;Independence March&quot;) is the national anthem of the <b>Republic of Turkey</b> and of the Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus.</blockquote><a href="/songs/istiklal-marsi">Independence March</a></li></ul></section>
